# 20. Testing and Acceptance Criteria

The project is not complete merely because the homepage looks correct.

### Frontend

- All public routes render correctly.
- Desktop and mobile navigation work.
- Event search and filters work.
- Day selection updates the booking summary.
- Quantity controls work.
- Cart items can be added, updated and removed.
- Seat selection reflects actual availability where supported.
- All buttons have a defined action.
- Loading, empty and error states exist.

### Backend

- Protected endpoints reject missing or invalid authentication.
- Customers cannot read other customers' orders.
- Unauthorized users cannot access admin endpoints.
- Server-calculated totals cannot be overridden by the browser.
- Inventory cannot be oversold through concurrent reservations.
- Expired reservations release inventory correctly.
- Duplicate webhooks do not create duplicate orders or tickets.
- Email failures can be retried safely.
- Refunds are reflected consistently across payment, order and ticket records.

### Admin

- Authorized staff can create and publish events.
- Ticket prices and inventory can be updated.
- Customer and order searches work.
- Payment references are visible to authorized staff.
- Refund actions require the appropriate permission.
- Marketing preferences and unsubscribe status are respected.
- Sensitive operations appear in audit logs.

### Launch gate

The application cannot be considered production-ready until payment testing, inventory concurrency testing, access-control testing, backup recovery and authorized ticket-delivery testing have passed.

